  "interiorEntryX": 10,
  "interiorEntryY": 13,
  "npcs": [
    {
      "id": "npc_thalorax_silt",
      "name": "Depth-Warden Silt",
      "spriteName": "npcs/guard",
      "type": "QUESTGIVER",
      "defaultDialog": "The deep remembers what the surface forgets.",
      "questCompleteDialog": "",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "start",
        "nodes": {
          "start": {
            "id": "start",
            "text": "[A figure in barnacle-crusted armor stands watching the darkness.] You have descended to the Abyssal Depths. I am Silt, warden of the pressure wards. Thalorax's domain is not kind to visitors.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What is this place?",
                "nextNodeId": "explain"
              },
              {
                "label": "I seek the Key of Depths.",
                "nextNodeId": "key_ask"
              },
              {
                "label": "Do you have one of the ward fragments yourself?",
                "nextNodeId": "silt_ward",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "FLAG_NOT_SET",
                    "target": "silt_gave_fragment",
                    "value": "",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "A child in Brightcoral wants to know what stone you set for someone who only left.",
                "nextNodeId": "silt_stone",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "QUEST_COMPLETE",
                    "target": "brightcorals_first_stone",
                    "value": "",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "FLAG_NOT_SET",
                    "target": "silt_told_stone",
                    "value": "",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "I can handle it.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "explain": {
            "id": "explain",
            "text": "The Crushing Deep. Thalorax sank his domain beneath the waves after the Shattering. He believes that truth is found only under pressure — that what survives compression is worthy. The wards keep the worst of it at bay, but they're cracking.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "The wards are failing?",
                "nextNodeId": "wards"
              },
              {
                "label": "I'll be careful.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "wards": {
            "id": "wards",
            "text": "Three ward fragments have drifted into the deep currents. Without them, the pressure dome over Abyssport will collapse. The Drowned Engineer in the city knows more — speak with her.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "I'll find the Engineer.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "thalorax_wards_warned",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "key_ask": {
            "id": "key_ask",
            "text": "The Key of Depths is earned in Thalorax's trial, deep in the Pressure Temple to the south. But first you must understand what he values: endurance, sacrifice, and the willingness to be crushed and reformed.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Where is the Pressure Temple?",
                "nextNodeId": "temple_dir"
              },
              {
                "label": "I'm ready.",
                "nextNodeId": "farewell"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "temple_dir": {
            "id": "temple_dir",
            "text": "South, past the pressure vents, beyond the boneyard. You will see the ward-ring — a circle of glowing runes. The temple entrance lies within. The abyssal wraiths grow thicker near it. Be prepared.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Thank you, Silt."
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "farewell": {
            "id": "farewell",
            "text": "The deep is patient. It has all the time in the world to crush you. [He turns back to watching the darkness.]",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "silt_ward": {
            "id": "silt_ward",
            "text": "One. It has been in my pack for nine years because I could never decide whether carrying it to Abyssport was my post or an excuse to leave it.\n[He hands it over, and looks lighter by more than its weight.] You decide for me. That is what you people are for.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_ITEM",
                "target": "pressure_ward_fragment",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 1
              },
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "silt_gave_fragment",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "silt_stone": {
            "id": "silt_stone",
            "text": "[The barnacled helm turns. He takes a long time, and the darkness he was watching goes on being watched by nobody.]\nThe same stone. She sets the same stone she would set for a drowning.\nBut she will have to keep setting it. That is the difference, and it is the whole difference. The drowned are finished; you set their stone once and the reef holds it up for you afterwards. Somebody who only went away keeps on not being dead, every morning, for as long as the child lives. Nobody holds that stone up but her.\nTell her I said it is heavier. Do not tell her it is not worth doing.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "silt_told_stone",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "x": 58,
      "y": 92
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_thalorax_lure",
      "name": "Lure",
      "spriteName": "npcs/fisher",
      "type": "TOWNSFOLK",
      "defaultDialog": "...the light shows the way down...",
      "questCompleteDialog": "",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "start",
        "nodes": {
          "start": {
            "id": "start",
            "text": "[A pale child sits cross-legged on the ocean floor. A faint bioluminescent glow pulses from her forehead.] ...you followed the light too? Everyone follows the light.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What is that light?",
                "nextNodeId": "light"
              },
              {
                "label": "Are you all right?",
                "nextNodeId": "okay"
              },
              {
                "label": "Oleander needs lumen coral for the Brightcoral lamp.",
                "nextNodeId": "lure_lumen",
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "type": "QUEST_ACTIVE",
                    "target": "the_undrowned_lamp",
                    "value": "",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "FLAG_NOT_SET",
                    "target": "lure_gave_lumen",
                    "value": "",
                    "amount": 0,
                    "negate": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "label": "Goodbye.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "light": {
            "id": "light",
            "text": "Thalorax gave it to me. He said I was brave for coming down so deep. The light shows me things in the dark — old bones, old ships, old truths. Things people tried to sink.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "What kind of truths?",
                "nextNodeId": "truths"
              },
              {
                "label": "Be careful down here.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "truths": {
            "id": "truths",
            "text": "The kind people bury. Seraphine came this way once — I saw her footprints in the sand. She was looking for something the gods hid. The Pressure Temple has her journal... if the wraiths haven't eaten the pages.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Thank you, Lure.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "lure_seraphine_hint",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "okay": {
            "id": "okay",
            "text": "The pressure doesn't bother me anymore. I think I'm becoming part of the deep. Like the coral becomes part of the reef. It's not scary. It's just... inevitable.",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Stay safe, little one.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "bye": {
            "id": "bye",
            "text": "[The glow on her forehead pulses once, illuminating the dark water around you.] Follow the bioluminescent sand. It's the safe path. Mostly.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "lure_lumen": {
            "id": "lure_lumen",
            "text": "The old lamp lady? [The glow on her forehead dips, thinking.] Thalorax gave me mine. He said I was brave for coming down so deep. I've had it four years and I've never once turned it off, because I didn't know you were allowed to.\n...You can turn it off?\n[She reaches up and works the coral free with both hands, and it comes away easier than it should, and the dark closes over her face and she is only a child sitting on the sand.]\nOh. Oh, that's better. It was so loud.\nTake it to her. Tell her a brave girl sent it and she can have it, but she has to actually use it for something, not just keep it.",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "GIVE_ITEM",
                "target": "lumen_coral",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 1
              },
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "lure_gave_lumen",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "LOG_MESSAGE",
                "target": "Lure works the light out of her forehead and hands it over.",
                "value": "GOOD",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "x": 105,
      "y": 110
    },
    {
      "id": "npc_thalorax_jaw",
      "name": "The Leviathan's Jaw",
      "spriteName": "npcs/sage",
      "type": "TOWNSFOLK",
      "defaultDialog": "[Ancient bones hum with residual power.]",
      "questCompleteDialog": "",
      "shopItemIds": [],
      "dialogueTree": {
        "startNodeId": "start",
        "nodes": {
          "start": {
            "id": "start",
            "text": "[You stand before the fossilized jaw of an ancient leviathan. Runes carved into the bone glow faintly.] The bones whisper: 'We were the first to sink. We were the first to understand.'",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Touch the runes.",
                "nextNodeId": "touch"
              },
              {
                "label": "Read the inscriptions.",
                "nextNodeId": "read"
              },
              {
                "label": "Step back.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": []
          },
          "touch": {
            "id": "touch",
            "text": "[A vision floods your mind: a world before the Shattering, leviathans swimming through crystal seas, and Thalorax — not a god of crushing darkness, but a guardian of the deep's wonders. Then the Shattering came, and wonder became pressure, became survival, became inevitability.]",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "[Release the bone.]",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "thalorax_leviathan_vision",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              },
              {
                "type": "LOG_MESSAGE",
                "target": "A vision of the world before the Shattering fills your mind.",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "read": {
            "id": "read",
            "text": "The inscriptions are old — older than the gods’ current forms. They speak of Aqualon, the drowned world beneath the world, and of the seven dreams it dreamed that woke and turned on it. What the forge-priests call the Forge Eternal, these stones call Aqualon’s dreaming, and the shards its broken sleep. “What sinks is not lost. What is crushed is made diamond. Thalorax remembers the weight of truth.”",
            "choices": [
              {
                "label": "Interesting.",
                "nextNodeId": "bye"
              }
            ],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "SET_FLAG",
                "target": "read_leviathan_inscription",
                "value": "true",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "bye": {
            "id": "bye",
            "text": "[The runes dim. The boneyard is silent once more.]",
            "choices": [],
            "actions": [
              {
                "type": "CLOSE_DIALOGUE",
                "target": "",
                "value": "",
                "amount": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "x": 115,
      "y": 160
    }
  ],
